Turns off the fix in the simulator's I2 checker (commit 031e7aa, DESIGN.md
§14.1 I2): `follow` in crates/sim/src/sim.rs no longer moves a node's
adoption of some content to the conflict-copy path sync displaced it to,
so the adoption stays at the path and time it was made. The user deleting
or rewriting the copy is then no longer the user's own change, and I2
reports it as sync losing the content. The engine is unchanged; only the
checker's bookkeeping is.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_conflict_copy_its_user_mass_deleted_is_not_lost
test: delocal-sim sim::tests::an_adoption_follows_its_content_to_the_conflict_copy

